  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="commodity_mantelle_cb179fb7b3cacafa089938c519ffcbe337506e5712f9166136eebf7af2b13b3804">
    <crm:P190_has_symbolic_content>a mantle of furs: a number of furs sewn together to make a fur lining, usually (by the 15th century) of a standard size (Veale 220)

Note that mantles are also a form of cloak. </crm:P190_has_symbolic_content>
